WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
The word says RED. The ink tells another story. Why is naming the ink unexpectedly difficult?

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:14.000
For a skilled reader, a word can compete with an instruction even when reading is not the goal.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:21.000
Researchers gave selected volunteers an unusual suggestion: regard the words as meaningless marks.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:28.000
Their interference fell. In one study, a formal hypnotic induction was not necessary for the change.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:35.000
That is an experiment about a specific task in highly suggestible people, not proof that an audio program fixes attention.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:42.000
Read the evidence. Try a free reflection exercise. Decide what a product is actually offering.
